  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Ward Round Notebook",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Ward Round Notebook\"**\n\nMedWise looks like the notebook a careful senior keeps on rounds: navy ink on white, written for a doctor between patients. Teal marks the answer or the live trace, and gold marks the point worth remembering. The ECG paper, pink-grid and warm, is the one place the page changes material, because that is where the reading happens.\n\nThe system is calm and exact rather than loud. One sans-serif family (Chivo) carries everything from the hero to the caliper readout, with Chivo Mono for numbers that are measured. Density follows the surface. The landing page breathes, with one idea per screen. The ECG course is a narrow, card-based column built for short sessions on a phone. The clinical tools put scanability first. Depth is a hairline border plus a very soft navy shadow, never a heavy drop shadow.\n\nThe `/app` sepsis tool still uses an older look: Inter with Libre Baskerville, blue `#004a80`, and square uppercase buttons with wide letter-spacing. That look is **legacy**. New work on `/app` moves it toward this system and never extends the old look.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy ink on white and cool grey; teal and gold used sparingly and with meaning",
      "One type family (Chivo), with Chivo Mono for measured values",
      "Soft corners on one scale (8 / 12 / 20 px)",
      "Hairline borders and faint navy-tinted shadows; flat at rest",
      "ECG paper as the single warm surface",
      "Real clinical material (real ECGs, real guideline rules) as the imagery"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Job Rule",
        "body": "Teal means \"this is the answer / this is live / this is active\"; gold means \"remember this / this is premium\". A colour used outside its job is a bug.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Warm Paper Rule",
        "body": "ECG paper pink appears only under an ECG tracing. No other surface is warm.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Measured Mono Rule",
        "body": "A number that came from a calliper, a clock or a score is set in Chivo Mono. Prose numbers stay in Chivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Single Family Rule",
        "body": "No second display face. Serif and \"font-display\" classes map to Chivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lift Means Link Rule",
        "body": "Only something you can click lifts. Static cards never move.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** set all text in Ward Navy (`#1a1c49`) or Slate Muted (`#5f6485`). Teal text on white must use Monitor Teal Ink (`#0b7466`).",
      "**Do** keep one primary (navy) button per view and pair it with at most one secondary.",
      "**Do** put every ECG on ECG paper with the 5 mm / 1 mm grid, at 25 mm/s and 10 mm/mV.",
      "**Do** set measured values (bpm, ms, timers, scores) in Chivo Mono with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** use the 8 / 12 / 20 px radius scale and the 4-to-128 px spacing scale; nothing in between.",
      "**Do** keep a visible 2 px teal focus ring on every interactive element and honour `prefers-reduced-motion`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** extend the legacy `/app` look (Inter, Libre Baskerville, `#004a80`, square uppercase buttons with wide tracking) to any new screen.",
      "**Don't** use Monitor Teal (`#18ab97`) as body text on white; it fails contrast.",
      "**Don't** use Chart Gold for anything but highlights and Pro markers.",
      "**Don't** use warm or pink surfaces anywhere except under an ECG.",
      "**Don't** add heavy drop shadows, gradients on buttons or glassy blur panels.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface.",
      "**Don't** make static cards lift on hover."
    ]
  }
}